{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"As of **2026-11-06**, establish these USD budgets and contractual allocations:\n\n- **One-time—normally sponsor:** formation, counsel, filings, listing/setup, initial service-provider onboarding, launch marketing and organizational-cost reimbursements.\n- **Recurring—sponsor/adviser under the unitary arrangement:** platform charges/minimums, administration, custody, transfer agency, accounting, audit, ordinary legal/compliance, trustees, insurance, exchange fees, index licensing and portfolio management. Separately budget sponsor distribution, marketing and overhead; identify bundled versus additional charges.\n- **Fund/shareholders:** the unitary advisory fee plus prospectus-defined exclusions—typically trading commissions, taxes, interest, acquired-fund expenses and specified extraordinary expenses. Confirm actual exclusions and contractual responsibility; “unitary” does not mean all-inclusive.\n- **Seed:** invested capital receiving ETF shares, not launch expenditure; track ownership, liquidity, market risk and eventual exit separately.\n\n**Worth knowing:** Break-even AUM equals annual fixed sponsor costs divided by a **positive retained fee margin** after variable/platform/advisory costs, using consistent units. Launch-cost recovery requires additional cumulative profit; seed recovery is separate."}}
